{"id":32250,"slug":"citizen-kane","title":"Citizen Kane","year":1941,"country":"United States","duration":119,"spine":1104,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/32250-citizen-kane","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/5e58f4effd7ec074436c3cefccc76e6f/Yp6qC4kg4JLjjqcNdK8RAVM8eK2qnR_large.jpg","description":"In the most dazzling debut feature in cinema history, twenty-five-year-old writer-producer-director-star Orson Welles synthesized the possibilities of sound-era filmmaking into what could be called the first truly modern movie. In telling the story of the meteoric rise and precipitous fall of a William Randolph Hearst–like newspaper magnate named Charles Foster Kane, Welles not only created the definitive portrait of American megalomania, he also unleashed a torrent of stylistic innovations—from the jigsaw-puzzle narrative structure to the stunning deep-focus camera work of Gregg Toland—that have ensured that Citizen Kane remains fresh and galvanizing for every new generation of moviegoers to encounter it.In the first manufacturing run of Citizen Kane, there was an issue with Blu-ray disc 1 of all of our editions. Corrected stock is available as of January 19, and if you made a purchase prior to this date, see the Current post below for more information on how to exchange your Blu-ray disc 1. ","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Orson Welles","slug":"orson-welles"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Orson Welles","role":"Charles Foster Kane","slug":"orson-welles"},{"actor":"Joseph Cotten","role":"Jedediah Leland","slug":"joseph-cotten"},{"actor":"Dorothy Comingore","role":"Susan Alexander Kane","slug":"dorothy-comingore"},{"actor":"Agnes Moorehead","role":"Mary Kane","slug":"agnes-moorehead"},{"actor":"Ruth Warrick","role":"Emily Monroe Norton Kane","slug":"ruth-warrick"},{"actor":"Ray Collins","role":"Jim W. Gettys","slug":"ray-collins"},{"actor":"Erskine Sanford","role":"Herbert Carter","slug":"erskine-sanford"},{"actor":"Everett Sloane","role